Draws a translated element, and everything in it, moved by its
translation, and finds it there for clicks; cuts an element with
clip-path or clip to its clip box; draws nothing of one with opacity 0. And a percentage height in a block
whose height is auto is auto, as CSS has it, not a percentage of the
viewport - Wikipedia's logo, height: 100% in its header, made the
header as tall as the window.

